      jsxRuntime.jsx(dataApp.RichNarrative, { id: "story:intro", value: story("story:intro", "## Intro\n\nMy Quant project began with small scripts and questions that I could express in a single comparison. A threshold was an accessible starting point: compare a closing price with a fixed absolute level. As the project grew, the question changed from where a price sat on an absolute scale to where it sat relative to a changing local context.\n\nThe first stage uses the **probability density function (PDF) of closing prices**, in the original price units. The second uses **STD**, a signed deviation measured in local standard-deviation units, to form a three-dimensional state-space view."),} )
