        jsxRuntime.jsx(dataApp.RichNarrative, { id: "threshold:body", value: story("threshold:body", "## The threshold stage: the PDF was a distribution of prices\n\nThe early workflow combined descriptive price analysis with fixed-level comparisons. A density analyzer **loads closing prices, selects a historical sample, estimates a Gaussian KDE, and locates its density peak**. A separate comparison uses a fixed price threshold. These have different roles: the density describes the sample; the threshold defines a boundary.\n\n### What the PDF describes\n\nThe density is over **price levels themselves**, not returns or percentage changes. A Gaussian kernel spreads each observed price into a small smooth contribution; adding those contributions reveals where prices were concentrated in the selected sample. The highest point is the estimated mode, not a forecast or an automatically justified decision boundary.\n\n### Reading the price distribution\n\nThe figure uses **1,212 closing-price observations** from an archived sample ending at its last observation, evaluated on a **1,000-point density grid**. Prices stay in their original units, and the horizontal axis spans the sample's minimum and maximum."),} )
